# Example doc map.
#
# A doc map points the app at source documents wherever they live on disk
# without copying them into one folder. Open via the "Open Doc Map" button
# in the left panel; you'll then pick an output directory where the
# project database (project.db) lives.
#
# Syntax:
#   - Each non-blank, non-comment line is a path or glob pattern.
#   - Lines starting with '!' EXCLUDE files matching the pattern.
#   - '~' expands to your home directory; '$VAR' expands to env vars.
#   - Relative paths resolve from the doc map file's directory.
#   - '**' recurses into subdirectories; '*' matches one path segment.
#   - Files with unsupported extensions are silently skipped.
#
# Example: research papers + project notes, excluding drafts.

# Include
~/Papers/2024/**/*.pdf
~/Papers/2025/**/*.pdf
~/Notes/**/*.md
./local-handouts/*.docx

# Exclude
!~/Papers/**/draft/**
!~/Notes/private/**
